  actors: 020000000300000002000000010000000200000001000000030000000200000001000000030000000100000002000000010000000300000001000000030000000100000003000000010000000100000003000000020000000100000002000000
  Dialogue:
  - 'Jenni? I thought you disappeared!

'
  - "Not Jenni exactly. Her spirit was too fractured. This is a friend, they\u2019ve
    taken over Jenni\u2019s form to help! \r\n"
  - "Oh\u2026 a pity. Well, simply put, the car won\u2019t start\r\n"
  - 'So? (Don''t get how fixing a toy car is supposed to solve apocalyptic issue)
    What do I gotta do about that? (I''ll just do what they tell me for now)

'
  - "Don't mistake this as me needing you or divine intervention or anyone else for
    that matter for anything but if it wasn\u2019t as obvious as it should\u2019ve
    been before: you need to find the starter"
  - I gathered but what the hell's is a starter?
  - Language!
  - Certainly, Divine Yota - how uncouth! The starter is something that st-
  - Starts the car. I got it wise guy but, what is that, exactly? Engine? Key?
  - "Wow, I didn\u2019t know your kind knew so much about cars, being non-human,
    a hermit and all.\r\n"
  - 'Have a little faith, peanut.

'
  - "If you\u2019re all quite finished\u2026 No, the starter is nothing like that.
    It\u2019s like a key: when pushed into the correct slot it gives the car power
    to start."
  - "Mhmm a key, huh? Last I checked\u2026 Toy cars don\u2019t have keys.\r\n"
  - "That\u2019s because it probably doesn\u2019t. What might be considered one thing
    here is likely referred to as something else out there. "
  - "well, that\u2019s just real dandy. Do you know what he\u2019s talking about?\r\n"
  - 'Mmm no. Real world vocabulary isn''t exactly on my list of duties.

'
  - What in the hell do you know exactly?
  - "Hey, I said watch the language! Remember you\u2019re talking to children\u2019s
    toys, for ages 2+. \r\n"
  - Jeez - my bad. Force of habit, y'know?
  - 'What in the heck am I supposed to do now? Better, butterfly?

'
  - '*sigh* I''ll allow it.'
  - "Since you lot are so incompetent, I\u2019ve perused the manual: it goes in underneath
    car. They come in pairs, one missing.  "
  - "\"Ages 2\" and he can say \u201Cperuse\u201D but I can\u2019t say h-"
  - 'Run along now. I have work to do.

'
